From 88c3b3fa08660ab8ab482f1f7ece594eafd3219c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Ojansivu <x@xet7.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:39:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [TZRES] Add Finnish (fi-FI) time zone names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: The time zone list of the Date and Time settings showed its
names in English on a Finnish system.

Why: The registry's MUI time zone values point at tzres's strings, and
tzres had only English.

How: Add lang/fi-FI.rc with every string of tzres.rc, by the same ids:
"Länsi-Euroopan normaaliaika", "... kesäaika", and display names with
the cities as Finnish writes them - "(UTC+02:00) Helsinki, Kiova, Riika,
Sofia, Tallinna, Vilna". Include it under LANGUAGE_FI_FI.
---
 dll/win32/tzres/lang/fi-FI.rc | 435 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dll/win32/tzres/tzres.rc      |   5 +
 2 files changed, 440 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 dll/win32/tzres/lang/fi-FI.rc

diff --git a/dll/win32/tzres/lang/fi-FI.rc b/dll/win32/tzres/lang/fi-FI.rc
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..7784193ca52
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dll/win32/tzres/lang/fi-FI.rc
@@ -0,0 +1,435 @@
